          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "If a quantity is decaying exponentially, then the ",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "half-life",
              "marks": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " of the quantity is the time required for it to halve in size.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p27-q6-task",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "fontSize": null,
          "align": "left",
          "spaceBefore": 0,
          "spaceAfter": 1,
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The half-life of carbon-14 is approximately 5730 years. Humans began agriculture approximately ten thousand years ago. If we had 1 kg of carbon-14 at that moment, then how much carbon-14, in grams, would we have now? Give your answer to the nearest gram.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Approximately $298$ grams.",
      "worked": "Let $M(t)$ be the mass in grams after $t$ years. The initial mass is $1000$ grams, and the mass halves every $5730$ years.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}M(t)&=1000\\left(\\frac12\\right)^{t/5730}\\\\M(10000)&=1000\\left(\\frac12\\right)^{10000/5730}\\\\M(10000)&\\approx298\\text{ g}.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 38
  },
